      ],
      "imageAt": [
        0,
        0.455
      ],
      "seconds": 19.72,
      "text": "Your eyes do not glide. They jump, several times a second, and during every jump the image smears into useless streaks. You never see that smear. Your brain cuts it out and stitches the two clean ends together, then backdates the result so the gap disappears. Add the cuts up and it is a meaningful slice of your waking day, deleted.",
      "delivery": {
        "rate": 8,
        "pitch": 0
      },
      "clips": [
